{"term":"yawn","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:891e5afb55c06dc0c2","definition":"To open the mouth widely and take a long, rather deep breath, often because one is tired or bored, and sometimes accompanied by pandiculation.","example":"I could see my students yawning, so I knew the lesson was boring them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:de7fc2e1fc122cb1ef","definition":"To say while yawning.","example":"“I haven’t the least idea what I want to do,” he yawned.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aeb90c5c771d6da231","definition":"To present a wide opening; gape.","example":"The canyon yawns as it has done for millions of years, and we stand looking, dumbstruck.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b98d1220cf36377673","definition":"To open the mouth, or to gape, through surprise or bewilderment.","example":"[…] O heavy hour!\nMethinks it should be now a huge eclipse\nOf sun and moon, and that the affrighted globe\nShould yawn at alteration.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25c5e8cfe0f7562aea","definition":"To be eager; to desire to swallow anything; to express desire by yawning.","example":"to yawn for fat livings","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f5a0dcf5caff6cf401","definition":"The action of yawning; opening the mouth widely and taking a long, rather deep breath, often because one is tired or bored.","example":"At length, quite exhausted by the attempt to be amused with her own book, which she had only chosen because it was the second volume of his, she gave a great yawn and said, “How pleasant it is to spend an evening in this way! […]”","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly","multicolour yawn","Technicolor yawn","yawnfest","yawnless","yawn-sigh","yawnsome","yawny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e525c1aa6fbf0c4675","definition":"A particularly boring event.","example":"The slideshow we sat through was such a yawn. I was glad when it finished.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly","multicolour yawn","Technicolor yawn","yawnfest","yawnless","yawn-sigh","yawnsome","yawny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c654f727fc0df2139f","definition":"A surname.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly","multicolour yawn","Technicolor yawn","yawnfest","yawnless","yawn-sigh","yawnsome","yawny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Yawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/jɔːn/"},"wordFamily":["yawnable","yawner","yawningly","multicolour yawn","Technicolor yawn","yawnfest","yawnless","yawn-sigh","yawnsome","yawny"]}